<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 21 June, from 217 BCE to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hannibal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/217-bce">217 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,242 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hannibal ambushes a Roman army at Lake Trasimene</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In morning mist on the lake shore, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> trapped the consul Flaminius's army, killing about 15,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>. The disaster led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> to appoint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-fabius-maximus">Fabius Maximus</a> as dictator.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1128">1128 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">898 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Clito defeats Thierry of Alsace at Axspoele</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-clito">William Clito</a>, imposed as Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-vi-of-france">Louis VI of France</a> after the murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-good">Charles the Good</a>, defeated his rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thierry-of-alsace">Thierry of Alsace</a> at Axspoele. Clito died at the siege of Aalst that year, and Thierry became count.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-clito">William Clito</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thierry-of-alsace">Thierry of Alsace</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1307">1307 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">719 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Külüg Khan is enthroned as emperor of the Yuan Dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Khayishan was enthroned as Külüg Khan, Emperor Wuzong of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. He is regarded as the seventh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>, though the title was only nominal because the empire had divided.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">Khagan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1529">1529 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">497 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An Imperial–Spanish army destroys the French at Landriano</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Antonio de Leyva's Imperial–Spanish army destroyed the French army of the Count of Saint-Pol at Landriano in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cognac">War of the League of Cognac</a>. It temporarily ended the struggle between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a> and Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> for control of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cognac">War of the League of Cognac</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1749">1749 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">277 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward Cornwallis founds Halifax, Nova Scotia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British settlers arrived to build a fortified town as a counterweight to French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisbourg">Louisbourg</a>. Halifax became a key naval base for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and later for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1788">1788 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">238 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New Hampshire's ratification puts the US Constitution into effect</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hampshire">New Hampshire</a> became the ninth state to ratify, the number required for the Constitution to take effect. The new federal government began work in 1789.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1791">1791 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">235 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis XVI and his family attempt to flee Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the night of 20–21 June, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a> and the royal family tried to leave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montmedy">Montmédy</a>, where he hoped to regain his freedom. Recognised at Sainte-Menehould, they were stopped and arrested at Varennes-en-Argonne.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1813">1813 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">213 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wellington routs Joseph Bonaparte at Vitoria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wellington">Wellington</a>'s Anglo-Portuguese and Spanish army broke the French in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, capturing their baggage train. Joseph fled, and French rule in Spain collapsed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1964">1964 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Three civil rights workers are murdered in Mississippi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">James Chaney, Andrew Goodman and Michael Schwerner were killed by Klansmen, with the involvement of local law officers, during Freedom Summer. Their deaths spurred support for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voting-rights-act-of-1965">Voting Rights Act of 1965</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 21 June <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-ix"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-leo-ix.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Leo IX</span><span class="tp">1002–1054</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-v-the-chaste"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/boleslaw-v-the-chaste.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bolesław V the Chaste</span><span class="tp">1226–1279</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-christian-baur"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-christian-baur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand Christian Baur</span><span class="tp">1792–1860</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/machado-de-assis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/machado-de-assis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Machado de Assis</span><span class="tp">1839–1908</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/damrong-rajanubhab"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/damrong-rajanubhab.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Damrong Rajanubhab</span><span class="tp">1862–1943</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lluis-companys"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lluis-companys.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lluís Companys</span><span class="tp">1882–1940</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/benazir-bhutto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/benazir-bhutto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Benazir Bhutto</span><span class="tp">1953–2007</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 21 June <span class="n">11</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fulk-nerra"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fulk-nerra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fulk Nerra</span><span class="tp">c. 970–1040</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-swabia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philip-of-swabia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Philip of Swabia</span><span class="tp">1177–1208</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wenceslaus-ii-of-bohemia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wenceslaus-ii-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Wenceslaus II of Bohemia</span><span class="tp">1271–1305</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-iii-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward III of England</span><span class="tp">1312–1377</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-ii-le-maingre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jean-ii-le-maingre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jean II Le Maingre</span><span class="tp">1366–1421</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/niccolo-machiavelli"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/niccolo-machiavelli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Niccolò Machiavelli</span><span class="tp">1469–1527</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/piero-strozzi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/piero-strozzi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Piero Strozzi</span><span class="tp">c. 1510–1558</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/aloysius-gonzaga"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aloysius-gonzaga.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Aloysius Gonzaga</span><span class="tp">1568–1591</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-smith-explorer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-smith-explorer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Smith (explorer)</span><span class="tp">1580–1631</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Antonio López de Santa Anna</span><span class="tp">1794–1876</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sukarno"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sukarno.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sukarno</span><span class="tp">1901–1970</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
